            type: "markdown-text"
            mode: "markdown"
            content: "## Overview\n\nSthalam enables sovereign individuals to publish and distribute content on their own terms—without platforms, algorithms, or intermediaries.\n\n## Content Types\n\n### Websites\nBuild interactive multi-page websites using HUML (Human Markup Language):\n- **Visual Builder**: Design websites with blocks (text, headings, images, markdown, HTML)\n- **Navigation Flows**: Create page transitions and branching logic\n- **Custom Styling**: Apply CSS for complete design control\n- **Interactive Elements**: Add forms, comment threads, and navigation buttons\n\n### Micro-blogs\nPublish Twitter-like posts with discussions:\n- **Short-form Content**: Quick updates and thoughts\n- **Comment Threads**: Real-time collaborative discussions\n- **Subscriber Distribution**: Viewers poll node to receive updates\n\n### Newsletters\nDirect distribution without email platforms:\n- **Rich Content**: Formatted text, images, and markdown\n- **Subscriber Delivery**: Sent directly to all connected viewers\n- **Pull-Based Updates**: Viewers poll node to receive new content\n\n## Publishing Flow\n\n### Step 1: Content Creation\n1. **Generate HUML Template**: Use an LLM to generate HUML templates\n2. **Edit Content**: Use the properties panel to customize\n3. **Add Interactivity**: Insert forms and comment threads\n4. **Preview**: Review before publishing\n\n### Step 2: Publishing to Sovereign Node\n- **Cryptographic Ownership**: Root UCAN establishes ownership\n- **Encryption**: AES-256-GCM encryption at rest\n- **Node Storage**: Content stored on your sovereign node\n\n### Step 3: Generating Share Tokens\n- **Folder-Level Sharing**: Share entire content folders\n- **UCAN Tokens**: Generate time-limited access tokens\n- **Connection Strings**: Base64-encoded access credentials\n\n### Step 4: Distribution\nShare connection strings via:\n- Email, chat, social media\n- QR codes\n- Website embeds\n- Out-of-band communication\n\n## Security Properties\n\n- **Cryptographic Ownership**: Root UCAN provides mathematical proof\n- **Multi-Layer Encryption**: At rest and in transit\n- **Access Control**: UCAN tokens define viewer permissions\n- **Data Sovereignty**: You control your node and content"
            css: "background: white; padding: 40px; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); line-height: 1.8; color: #2d3748; font-size: 16px;"

