            type: "section-container"
            name: "Nav Container"
            css: "max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center;"
            children::
              - ::
                type: "nav-button"
                content: "← Back to Sthalam"
                targetContainerId: "sthalam-intro"
                css: "background: #667eea; color: white; padding: 10px 20px; border: none; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px; cursor: pointer;"
              - ::
                type: "heading"
                content: "Comment Threads"
                css: "color: #667eea; font-size: 24px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0;"

      - ::
        type: "section-container"
        name: "Content Container"
        css: "max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 60px 40px;"
        children::
          - ::
            type: "heading"
            content: "Comment Threads"
            css: "color: #1a202c; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 30px;"

          - ::
            type: "markdown-text"
            mode: "markdown"
            content: "## Overview\n\nComment threads in Sthalam enable real-time conversations between publishers and viewers, as well as between viewers themselves. A single document can have **multiple independent comment threads** in different locations.\n\n## How It Works\n\n### Local-First Architecture\n\n1. **Local Write First**: Comments written to local Yjs doc first (instant UI update)\n2. **State Vector Sync**: Participants exchange state vectors with node\n3. **Bidirectional**: Both viewer and node send state vectors and respond with diffs\n4. **Never Full Doc**: Only CRDT diffs transferred after initial sync\n\n### Permission Model: `crud/write`\n\nThe viewer's UCAN token contains write access:\n- ✅ **Can read** existing comments via state vector sync\n- ✅ **Can write** new comments\n- ✅ **Can update** own comments\n- ✅ **Bidirectional flow**: All participants exchange state vectors\n- ✅ **Multi-viewer support**: Viewers see each other's comments\n\n## Real-time Synchronization\n\n### Active Connections\n\n1. Viewer A writes comment to local → instant UI update\n2. Viewer A exchanges state vectors with node → node receives comment\n3. Publisher sends state vector to node → receives Viewer A's comment\n4. Publisher writes reply to local → instant UI update\n5. Other viewers poll and receive updates\n\n**Sub-Second Latency**:\n- Instant local writes (no network wait)\n- Frequent state vector exchanges\n- QUIC provides fast transport\n- Only missing updates transferred\n\n### Offline Resilience\n\n- Comments stored locally when offline\n- Synced to node when reconnected\n- CRDT ensures conflict-free merging\n\n## Multiple Threads Per Document\n\nAll threads stored in single `thread_comments_doc`:\n\n```javascript\n{\n  threads: {\n    \"section1_thread\": [\n      { author: \"viewer_a\", text: \"Great post!\", ... },\n      { author: \"publisher\", text: \"Thanks!\", ... }\n    ],\n    \"section2_thread\": [\n      { author: \"viewer_b\", text: \"Question...\", ... }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Use Cases\n\n### Blog Post Discussions\n- Multiple threads for different sections\n- Focused conversations by topic\n- Community discussions between viewers\n\n### Newsletter Feedback\n- Readers share thoughts\n- Other readers respond\n- Publisher acknowledges feedback\n\n### Q&A Sections\n- Viewers post questions\n- Publisher provides answers\n- Knowledge base builds over time\n\n### Community Building\n- Viewer-to-viewer discussions\n- Publisher moderation\n- Sovereign community without platform control\n\n## Technical Features\n\n- **CRDT Properties**: Conflict-free merging across multiple threads\n- **Awareness**: Optional presence indicators\n- **Moderation**: Publisher control over content\n- **Spam Prevention**: Rate limiting and token expiration\n- **Encryption**: AES-256-GCM for all comments"
